# Fixed-warmup single-owner performance admission review — 22 October 2026

**Decision: verified performance parity is not established across the fixed seven families against both controls. Keep the draft stack held.** The corrected-policy candidate has ordinary complete-operation median losses for both priority dense workloads against main and published 0.1.0, plus losses in long reflow, cold mounting, width-change measurement, and small repeated setters. Sparse publication, independent copy, prepared inspection, and repeated edit/read sequences retain substantial gains. These are separate facts; the gains and the aggregate Labs counts cannot offset a required family's losses. The decision does not rest on an isolated p95 or the historical 113 ms block.

## Identity and method

The frozen runtime is commit dec7509b3a18b2d71e27de023419f45c32fb10e7, candidate archive SHA-256 06fe22b7f05dceb27f59b2e82d33fab541c8cee04c37b1a1ccdf078f6ecdc9be and shipping shaper executable SHA-256 66e6c46357030d8457a8568af303d8552b16a68f0c3815877d01d634996bbffb. Controls are main commit 4e25a96a57462fef5ad0d19065a822695b480f60, archive bbb3375c08fb3db8186ec10e4b766b7170632f7601eb1ec0e90be0197f22eb20, and published 0.1.0 archive 6e2bf7bdef50ec528a4e4799b8f067e81335388265fbb4950cbbcf08f840581b. The freeze records Labs 0.9.0 harness digest 2ac59f1c44447be4d5061003f3df32a66c87952ca297e4a804544f16c09b1f5e across 444 inputs.

All three arms use the full suite, eight fresh-process blocks, single-call sampling, and explicit fixed-20 warmup. The original first-result invocation plus 20 additional untimed callbacks yields 21 untimed calls per block; every saved row records eight counts of 21. The candidate's complete 145-identity capture is reused as identical candidate.json bytes, SHA-256 ad1c04fa0149ee123f831f91f126f7dfe1515ae77b4e141a826f346556b47e3b, in both control comparisons. Main raw baseline SHA-256 is 3888a3d1826a2e81e4612a23bb6fbea93eadff564e1daf7308ff5d15b343f3b7; published is d55c73d93007177e32dc439b32120d2c359176f1eba98b72b4b90d74105c06de. All arms report Apple M4, arm64 Darwin and Node 24.18.0; these were sequential separate runs, not paired callbacks.

The values below are absolute elapsed milliseconds for the complete named callback. For each arm and operation, saved retained nanosecond samples are sorted and nearest-rank p50/p90/p95 is sample[ceil(q × N) − 1]. Labs' unchanged per-block trim already occurred before storage; I removed no further sample. The comparison's block-estimator percentages, its 5% classification floor, and its aggregate workload summary are not the admission rule. The prior conditional/one-warmup matrix remains preserved but cannot be numerically compared with these fixed-20 samples. [The full 145-row analysis](fixed20-admission-analysis.json) retains each arm's p50/p90/p95, sample count, minimum, maximum, and **all eight block medians and warmup counts**, including every adverse tail.

