The “first set” fixture builds and publishes an existing scene before timing, then repeatedly changes its first label between two texts. Its setter-only row excludes requested measurement and scene publication. It is not a cold first assignment. Conversely, rewrite 512 and publish 1024 include all their setters and scene publication. The 100-edit immediate-measurement row performs **100 edit → glyph.shape() publication → measure sequences** within a 1,000-label scene; it is not 100 reads followed by one final publication. These semantics follow benches/labs/package/prepared-operations.bench.ts and batching.bench.ts.

